<title>BELGIUM: EU clears MG control of Safic-Alcan.</title>
<headline>EU clears MG control of Safic-Alcan.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELSS 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had approved Metallgesellschaft AG's plan to acquire full control of Safic-Alcan SA by buying a further 43.9 percent stake from the EXOR Group.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement that the operation would not create or strengthen a dominant position in the market concerned, including natural and synthetic rubber and natural latex as well as tropical oils, since the company would face competition from strong global producers.</p>
<p>Prior to the acquisition by Metallgesellschaft Handel &amp; Beteiligungen AG (MG), Safic-Alcan was jointly controlled by MG and EXOR.</p>
<p>The Commission said that MG will launch a bid to acquire the rest of Safic-Alcan shares quoted at the Paris exchange.</p>
</text>
